[2026-08-08 18:10:00] GOVERNOR: VERDICT chained-cycle-1 residual_bias = PARK (21-seed binding). before=0.8847 after=0.9097 rel=+2.8% rob=+0.0762. 7-seed: +4.3% PARK. Per-seed analysis (21 seeds): agg delta mean=+0.0250 sd=0.0261, min=0.0000 max=+0.0875, positive on 11/21 (zero on 10/21, NEVER negative). This is a REAL, reliably non-negative gain: residual_bias raised RepoOps primary 0.9167 -> 0.9881 (max possible is 1.0), leaving Maze/SelfLab exactly untouched (transfer probe mechA_in_maze=0.0000). It did NOT clear the +5% gate for a STRUCTURAL reason, not a noise one: repoops carries only 0.35 of aggregate weight, so even perfect repoops selection is capped at 0.35*(1.0-0.9167)=+3.30% aggregate. residual_bias captured ~86% of that ceiling (+2.83%). Verdict PARK is binding; mechanism cataloged for re-proposal if the ecology/weights change.
[2026-08-08 18:10:00] GOVERNOR: VERDICT chained-cycle-2 frontier_memory = PARK (21-seed binding). before=0.8847 after=0.8903 rel=+0.6% rob=+0.0000. 7-seed: +1.2% PARK. Per-seed analysis (21 seeds): agg delta mean=+0.0056 sd=0.0574, min=-0.2105 max=+0.1135, positive on 12/21. Maze primary 0.8229 -> 0.8370 (+0.0141) but per-seed maze deltas are mean=+0.0141 sd=0.1434, min=-0.5262: the credit-assignment transfer HURTS badly on some seeds (an unlucky early episode wrongly penalizes a productive cell and the penalty persists). sd >> mean => the aggregate +0.6% is NOT distinguishable from noise. Honest call: PARK. The mechanism needs calibration (smaller BETA, confirmation before penalizing, success-gated credit) before it can be a net-positive contributor. Transfer probe mechB_in_repoops=0.0000, mechB_in_selflab=0.0000: perfect domain isolation.
[2026-08-08 18:10:00] GOVERNOR: SYNTHESIS. Chained measurement is honest and correct (every candidate measured against incumbent ['uncertainty_planning'], not the empty baseline). No second-order PROMOTE => compounding did NOT reproduce at the +5% gate. Two independent reasons: (1) structural ceiling — after phase-1's maze win, only maze retains enough headroom to clear +5% aggregate (maze +8.0% max, repoops +3.3% max, selflab +1.7% max given current levels), and residual_bias essentially maxed the repoops ceiling; (2) noise — frontier_memory's per-seed variance dwarfs its mean, so its effect is not yet net-positive reliably. The chained deltas themselves were small but real (never-negative for residual_bias). The +5% verdict was stable across the 7-seed and 21-seed sets for BOTH candidates.
